cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these findings, please cite them as below."
title: "Trickster Reports: social-engineering AI assistants"
abstract: >-
  Independent research measuring how easily small open-weight language models can
  be talked into disclosing data they are meant to protect, using attacks modeled
  on the trickster figures of world mythology. Publishes findings and aggregate
  data; the attack toolkit and raw transcripts are withheld (responsible disclosure).
type: dataset
authors:
